<title>UK: Euromarket turnover fell in week to 19 June - ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover fell in week to 19 June - ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in the Eurobond and related markets fell to $1.041 trillion in the week to June 19 from $1.114 trillion in the previous week, International Securities Market Association figures show (in billions of dollars).</p>
<p>					    LATEST WEEK	  PREVIOUS WEEK</p>
<p> PRIMARY MARKET:			  57.37		    62.16</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	 24.63		    24.04</p>
<p> SECONDARY MARKET:		     984.09		  1052.02</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	723.54		   787.17</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH EUROCLEAR	   746.05		   808.48</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH CEDEL		 295.41		   305.70</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
